# Unity AI – Project Progress

## Week 1: Research and Finding the Problem

We started by talking about problems that families face in daily life. We found problems such as busy schedules, forgetting tasks, not spending enough time together, and communication problems. We decided to create an app that uses AI to help families stay organized and connected.

## Week 2: Developing the Idea

After doing some research and discussing different ideas, we created **Unity AI**.

Our app is designed to help families with:

* Managing tasks
* Reminders
* Mood tracking
* Family support
* AI suggestions
* Communication

We planned how each feature could help families in their daily lives.

## Week 3: App Design

We planned how the app would work and how users would move between the pages. We wanted the app to be simple and easy for different family members to use.

We started designing the app using Figma and created the first version of the interface.

## Week 4: Prototype

We continued working on our Figma prototype and created the main pages, including:

* Home page
* Tasks page
* Mood tracking
* Family support
* AI suggestions

We also connected the pages to make the prototype interactive.

## Current Progress

We have finished the main idea, problem, solution, and basic app design. We are now improving the prototype and making the app easier to use.

We are also working on our presentation and demonstration video.

## Next Steps

* Improve the prototype
* Improve the AI suggestions
* Test the app
* Get feedback
* Finish the presentation and video

## Short GitHub Description

**Unity AI is a smart family support app that helps families stay organized and connected. It includes task management, mood tracking, reminders, and AI suggestions. Our goal is to use AI in a simple and useful way to help families in their daily lives.**
